lines=['# The Table: draft propositions','', 'Version 0.1 | 30 October 2026 | Internal design for user/client review; not an offer to send','', '## The proposal in one minute','','Build a useful payroll decision research edition first. A buyer receives defined research and use rights; a founding partner supports defined work and receives stated benefits; a practitioner contributes on a practical permitted basis and receives free research and relevant peer value. An event is a possible additional format, not a prerequisite for the first report.','', 'These drafts describe JGA’s potential future products. The signed project still delivers the complete commissioned report, feasibility assessment and agreed assets. It is not replaced with a smaller pack, and no recurring production, advice or events have been added to Riseklix’s obligations.','', '| Draft | Who it serves | Proposed minimum | What remains to test |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |','| TP01 Research-use pack | A payroll technology, outsourcing, HCM, consulting or investment organisation with a specific use | Dated edition, relevant reading path, actual evidence context and clear use definition | Does it resolve a real gap after public/internal alternatives? Is any extra briefing or client/public use wanted? |','| TP02 Founding research partnership | An organisation with a genuine reason to fund a defined edition | Edition, bounded findings briefing, accurate funding acknowledgement and agreed uses | Does that combination merit funding, on what evidence and without control of the findings? |','| TP03 Practitioner cycle | Relevant senior practitioners whose experience and peer exchange fit the research | Free research/free attendance as proposed, industry question, appropriate input and possible moderated exchange | Does it earn their time, fit employer/format conditions and offer value beyond hospitality? |','', '## TP01: Payroll Decision Evidence Pack','','The proposed starting point is the finished, dated edition with a short route through the relevant evidence, supported case contrasts and practical tools for the user’s actual task. The same edition may support different uses; it is not a new bespoke study for every customer. A scoped briefing or prepared client/public-use excerpt is an optional component to define and cost. No duration, turnaround, price or future-update promise is made.','', 'The five contract-named [buyer segments](T02-BUYER-USES-AND-RIGHTS.md) have different possible uses. Product/service strategy, a client brief and an investment research question should not be treated as the same purchase. Employer-side use is an additional hypothesis; participating practitioners already receive the research free. Preserve that benefit and do not count equivalent access twice.','', '**Concept wording after unaided discovery:**','',recs[0]['concept_after_discovery'],'', 'Change or stop this concept if the required evidence is absent, existing material already meets the need, or the customer requires representative statistics, private identities, a guaranteed result or a service JGA cannot supply.','', '## TP02: Founding Research Partnership','','One defined edition, a bounded briefing, accurate funding acknowledgement and agreed uses form the minimum combination to examine. Its value must come from a real research, strategy or communication use. A funding partner can help agree topic/focus beforehand; it does not buy favourable findings, suppression, method/results control or an implied endorsement. JGA retains final publication responsibility under the working agreement.','', 'Name the actual edition and funding purpose. If research is already commissioned or complete, describe that accurately and distinguish any additional release, briefing or distribution work; do not present it as a newly commissioned study. Keep production costs and partner/licence revenues separately defined, counting each cost and bundled entitlement once.','', 'A separately defined event/access component remains possible if transparent, wanted, permissioned and deliverable. It is absent from the minimum draft. Funding does not automatically provide participant contacts, individual answers, introductions, meetings or exclusivity.','', '**Concept wording after unaided discovery:**','',recs[1]['concept_after_discovery'],'', 'Change or stop if the economics depend on unagreed lead access, a target audience inconsistent with the research/member fit, editorial control, or benefits that cannot be delivered. General support for the idea is not a funding commitment.','', '## TP03: Practitioner research and peer cycle','','Preserve free attendance and free research, one industry question and optional council recognition from the original concept. The useful exchange to test is relevant evidence and peers, not simply premium dining. Not every proposed question can become a mandatory research question or receive a promised answer.','', 'One short follow-through note, separating useful takeaways from unresolved questions, is an additional benefit idea to test and cost. It is not a promised monthly output, advice desk or new obligation in the signed project. Recognition does not by itself authorise attendance disclosure or attribution; contextual details can still identify someone.','', '**Concept wording after unaided discovery:**','',recs[2]['concept_after_discovery'],'', 'Change or stop if participant/peer fit is weak, hospitality or contribution cannot be accepted, the format creates too much burden, or there is no useful return beyond the event. A permitted remote/written contribution may still be useful; it is neither event attendance nor automatically a usable report contribution.','', '## Event comparison','','Compare the same intended research/member benefit using research-only, remote/written exchange and a small UK in-person gathering. Identify what the gathering adds before assuming all research sales depend on dinners. The proposed four-city programme remains an option to assess later, with changing cohorts rather than a longitudinal panel. No venue, date, membership or launch is confirmed.','', '## What needs definition before a proposal','','Keep these as four grouped product decisions, not a long new participant form:','', '1. Actual user, decision and existing alternatives, including the contributor’s free research.','2. Specific edition, useful outputs, evidence limits and internal/client/public uses.','3. Responsible delivery owner, preparation/service limits, permissions and practical capacity.','4. Real commercial unit, complete costs, funding timing and separately agreed price/terms.','', 'JGA’s commissioned IP rights are governed by the working agreement. The [use options](T02-use-and-entitlement-options.json) are future customer-product choices, not a new Riseklix licence or veto. Underlying participant and third-party constraints still matter.','', '## Test it without turning discovery into a pitch','','Use the proposed [version 0.2 Table guides](../01-method/TABLE-VALIDATION-GUIDES-v0.2.md): actual recent needs/alternatives before showing a relevant short concept, research alone before asking what an event adds, then evidence/use/purchase-route/objections. Show only relevant options and record the actual version/order. All probes remain selective.','', 'The original Table guide remains in its file and the active WP03 policy is unchanged. This proposed version requires review before actual collection; it activates nothing. Up to four substantive Table contribution events, ideally two buyers/partners and two prospective members, remain separate from six-to-ten distinct eligible report contributors. Four conversations cannot establish market size, price elasticity or a conversion forecast.','', 'The [delivery/validation map](T02-DELIVERY-AND-VALIDATION.md) separates the work needed from evidence actually obtained. All actual customer, participant, permission, commitment, price and financial-input arrays remain empty. Current findings support a draft design; T03 validation and T04/T05 economics remain open.']
(R/'04-table/T02-PROPOSITION-PACK.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
work=[
('DW01','Research edition','Define audience/decision scope, collect actual evidence, code/review, write/design and finalise with rights/currentness checks.','Research and editorial owner; actual capacity not confirmed.','Versioned publishable evidence and complete contracted publication; do not count future sponsor-specific editions as already funded.'),
('DW02','Reading path and existing tools','Choose supported sections/contrasts and relevant existing framework/templates for the stated use.','Research/editorial preparation; actual hours unknown.','A short task-based route through the edition, without new bespoke study or invented case evidence.'),
('DW03','Bounded briefing if included','Set user/audience, agenda, preparation, format and follow-up boundary; identify a capable available person.','Briefing/service owner; no staffed analyst bench or time promise presumed.','Defined service and its complete labour cost; capacity and price assessed later.'),
('DW04','Use/recognition assets','Specify material/version, allowed use, source/participant constraints, funding statement and logo permissions where relevant.','JGA publication/commercial owner and appropriate rights review.','Actual agreed use/asset record; no default third-party rights or participant data access.'),
('DW05','Practitioner research/peer route','Screen relevant fit, choose practical input/meeting mode, apply existing permission and count policy.','Research/participation/moderation owner; tools and arrangements not approved by this map.','Actual eligible usable permitted contribution and separately tracked peer/event participation.'),
('DW06','Cycle follow-through if included','Prepare a short note with appropriate takeaways, limits and open questions; review for indirect identification.','Editorial/moderation follow-through capacity to test and cost.','A scoped optional benefit; no unlimited advice or recurring output.'),
('DW07','Event increment if chosen','Add recruitment, host/moderator seats, venue/hospitality, access, travel, timing and cancellation work.','Event/programme owner and funding; no supplier enquiry or booking made.','Incremental fully loaded resource/cash model against the research-only route, not all sales attributed to dinners.'),
('DW08','Sales/administration and later upkeep','Define proposal/contract/invoice/fulfilment/correction work, edition period and any genuinely chosen future refresh.','Commercial/administrative/editorial owners, not an assumed recurring team.','Count bundled licences once; distinguish contracted, invoiced, received and fulfilled; no automatic renewal.')]
wr('04-table/T02-delivery-map.json',dict(date=D,status='design_work_requirements_not_resource_plan',items=[dict(work_id=i,object=n,work=w,owner_role_requirement=o,completion_evidence=e,owner_assigned=False,hours=None,cash_cost=None,capacity_confirmed=False)for i,n,w,o,e in work],financial_inputs=[],actual_delivery_events=[],staff_hired=[],new_signed_project_deliverables=[],commercial_validation=False))
text=['# T02: delivery and validation map','', 'Internal design, 30October 2026. This maps work and evidence needs without inventing costs, staff availability or customer outcomes.','', '| Work object | Necessary work | Evidence of fulfilment to define |','| --- | --- | --- |']
for i,n,w,o,e in work:text.append(f'| {i}: {n} | {w} {o} | {e} |')
text+=['','## What future input can and cannot show','','Use the existing six buyer and six member questions selectively. A real prior purchase, actual decision and specific unmet evidence need are more informative than general enthusiasm. A request for a scoped proposal is a possible next decision; it is not a signed order. Receipt of money is not the same as delivery of a permissioned asset or useful benefit.','', '| Hypothesis | Useful input to seek | Counter-signal |','| --- | --- | --- |','| H01 Research use | Actual decision/user, alternatives, missing input and wanted output/use | Equivalent free/internal material is enough, or evidence cannot support the task |','| H02 Funding | Real use, acceptable independent evidence, purchase route and defined rights | Value depends on unagreed private access, favourable findings or unsuitable recruitment |','| H03 Practitioner value | Recent relevant need, peer fit, permitted practical input and valued follow-through | Time/permission/format prevents participation or value is hospitality only |','| H04 Event increment | Specific benefit over research-only/remote/written alternatives | Added travel/cost/burden with no distinct benefit or delivery/funding route |','', 'The existing Table cap is up to four substantive exploratory contribution events; variation is purposeful, not a representative survey. Preserve objections, unknowns and missing information. No success percentage, fixed validation score, price elasticity or market forecast is appropriate from this design.','', '## Readiness remains separate','','The [existing five release decisions](../01-method/collection-pack-v0.1/REVIEW-DECISIONS.json) remain unchanged and unconfirmed. They cover actual focus/timing/introduction, dataflow/access, JGA notice/instructions, output/use choices and user permission for the exact send/route. Neither this map nor the draft guide activates fieldwork.','', 'The proposed guide/version and concept shown should be linked to any later permitted record. Use approved restricted storage for identities, keep only appropriate analysis records here, and retain quote/paraphrase/interpretation distinctions. Existing counting/permission templates remain the basis; no duplicate identity store or new mandatory response form is created.','', '## Next work after this design review','','Use actual T03 input when collection is ready. Meanwhile T04/T05 can define commercial routes and gather appropriate public cost context, preserving assumption/source/unit/currency/tax/date and full JGA work. Pricing and a funded UK pilot decision come from the completed product, inputs and risk appetite, not competitor list-price averaging or the current USD1,500 commission. No price, financial input, source claim or actual research record has been added here.']
(R/'04-table/T02-DELIVERY-AND-VALIDATION.md').write_text('\n'.join(text)+'\n')
print('T02 three-proposition pack, delivery and structured maps written')
